config-connector-extensions patch 0013: mockgcp stores Cloud Storage objects with their content.

For storage.gcp.hfl.dev StorageBucketObject. Before, objects.get always
answered "no such object" and nothing served uploads. Written here:
- mockstorage/objectmedia.go serves uploads (POST
  /upload/storage/v1/b/{bucket}/o, uploadType media or multipart) into an
  existing bucket, each a new generation with its size, MD5 and CRC32C, and
  content reads (alt=media), beside the generated mux, as handleBucketIAM
  does; service.go calls it;
- objects.go: objects.get returns the stored object, and objects.delete
  deletes it and its content.
- mockgcp_http.go: prefilterRequest, which parses every request body as
  JSON, leaves /upload/ requests alone.
Resumable uploads are not served. Upstream candidate: yes.
